 ## Mapscripts
 
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6114+) **Optional XML-tunable BTS/AdvCiv standard-map generation:** AdvCiv-SAS's default map generation uses the shared [`CvMapGeneratorUtil.py`](/Assets/Python/CvMapGeneratorUtil.py) helpers and [`CvMapGenerator.cpp`](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvMapGenerator.cpp) DLL behavior inherited from base AdvCiv. New independent SAS defines let players select BTS alternatives for individual shared generation steps, including standard terrain and feature generation, fractal defaults, latitude, coastal Peaks, rivers, lakes, and bonus placement/distribution, without recompiling the DLL. The defaults continue to use AdvCiv's behavior because that remains the intended AdvCiv-SAS setting. These controls do not override separate Python map scripts, or undo the changes that AdvCiv-SAS has made to Terrain/Feature/Bonus XML Info and other map-related GlobalDefines. See the documented map-generation block in [`GlobalDefines_advciv_sas.xml`](/Assets/XML/GlobalDefines_advciv_sas.xml).
 - Modify **Highlands** so it supports AdvCiv-SAS's new world sizes. Also increase its players supported from 18 to 48+ (for the 48 civs DLL). Change in the new [Highlands.py](/PrivateMaps/Highlands.py). Grid size **computed dynamically beyond Huge**. See [SAS_WorldSizeUtils.py](/Assets/Python/SAS_WorldSizeUtils.py). See also: [Modding ressources (Mapscripts)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/Modding_Ressources/README.md#mapscripts).
 - Similarly also fix **other maps** to make them **compatible with AdvCiv-SAS**: [aDebugMap.py](/PrivateMaps/aDebugMap.py), [Fantasy_Realm.py](/PrivateMaps/Fantasy_Realm.py), [Great_Plains.py](/PrivateMaps/Great_Plains.py), [Ice_Age.py](/PrivateMaps/Ice_Age.py), [Inland_Sea.py](/PrivateMaps/Inland_Sea.py), [Lakes.py](/PrivateMaps/Lakes.py), [Maze.py](/PrivateMaps/Maze.py), [Hub.py](/PrivateMaps/Hub.py), [Mirror.py](/PrivateMaps/Mirror.py), [Oasis.py](/PrivateMaps/Oasis.py), [Ring.py](/PrivateMaps/Ring.py), [Team_Battleground.py](/PrivateMaps/Team_Battleground.py), [Tilted_Axis.py](/PrivateMaps/Tilted_Axis.py), [Wheel.py](/PrivateMaps/Wheel.py), [Arboria.py](/PrivateMaps/Arboria.py), [Donut.py](/PrivateMaps/Donut.py), [Earth2.py](/PrivateMaps/Earth2.py) (see below), [Global_Highlands.py](/PrivateMaps/Global_Highlands.py), [PerfectMongoose.py](/PrivateMaps/PerfectMongoose.py), [Rainforest.py](/PrivateMaps/Rainforest.py), [RandomScriptMap.py](/PrivateMaps/RandomScriptMap.py), [Terra.py](/PrivateMaps/Terra.py).
 - Added shared Mapscript-related world-size helpers. Note: done in [SAS_WorldSizeUtils.py](/Assets/Python/SAS_WorldSizeUtils.py) rather than in the [PrivateMaps](/PrivateMaps/) folder as a .py file. This is because such a previous design caused the helper-as-a-playable-mapscript related bug, in AdvCiv-SAS only, of RandomScriptMap and Archipelago, e.g. at Huge world size, being generated far too small (`60 x 44`). After the fix it returned to `120 x 84`, matching base AdvCiv visually at a glance, and not being overly cramped anymore. The same issue may also have affected other map scripts that imported the old helper. The old helper now only keeps the minimal new playable mapscript code, not imported by other mapscripts anymore, in the new **SAS_Simple_Flat_Grass**: a simple sandbox map with almost all land and mostly flat grass tiles. See [SAS_Simple_Flat_Grass.py](/PrivateMaps/SAS_Simple_Flat_Grass.py).

